# The working tree is checked out on macOS, Linux and Windows, and `rustfmt.toml`
# pins `newline_style = "Unix"`. Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`,
# which would rewrite every file to CRLF on checkout — `cargo fmt --check` then
# rejects every source file, and `script/bootstrap` becomes an unrunnable `sh`
# script with a `\r` in its shebang. Normalising here is what makes the file on
# disk the same bytes on all three.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be normalised.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
